# FWMS — Faculty Workload Management System: Complete System Blueprint

> **Generated from**: Exhaustive source code analysis of the FWMS repository  
> **Anti-hallucination policy**: All facts verified from repository files. Anything unverified is marked **UNKNOWN FROM REPOSITORY**.

---

## 1. System Purpose & Overview

The FWMS is a **dual-purpose academic management system** for a university department (Computer Applications — MCA/BCA programs at Hindustan University):

1. **FCFS Subject Selection** — Students/faculty select subjects through time-windowed FCFS (First-Come-First-Served) windows with advisory-lock-based concurrency control
2. **Faculty Workload Management** — Coordinators manage faculty preferences, run an automated allocation engine, override assignments, and generate workload reports

### Key Use Cases
- Faculty login via Google OAuth and submit ranked preferences (1–5) for subject offerings
- Coordinator opens/closes preference windows, runs allocation engine, overrides/reassigns allocations
- Coordinator freezes/unfreezes allocations, manages staff records and academic cycles
- Reports exported as Excel (3 sheets) or PDF

