## 3. Backend Architecture

### 3.1 Framework & Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Framework | **FastAPI** (Python 3.12) |
| Database | **PostgreSQL 15+** via **SQLAlchemy** (raw SQL, no ORM models) |
| Auth | **Google OAuth 2.0** + **PyJWT** + session cookies |
| Sessions | **Redis** (production) or **in-memory** (development) |
| Connection Pool | SQLAlchemy `create_engine` (pool_size=10, max_overflow=20) |
| Middleware | [CorrelationIDMiddleware](file:///c:/Users/itsni/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/faculty_selection/app/core/correlation_middleware.py#23-91) (UUID per request → `X-Correlation-ID`) |
| Exports | **openpyxl** (Excel), **reportlab** (PDF) |

### 3.2 Architectural Pattern

All modules follow: **Router → Service → Raw SQL (parameterized)**.  
No SQLAlchemy ORM models are used — all database access is via `sqlalchemy.text()` with named parameters.

### 3.3 Transaction Management

[app/db/session.py](file:///c:/Users/itsni/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/faculty_selection/app/db/session.py) — [get_transaction()](file:///c:/Users/itsni/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/faculty_selection/app/db/session.py#20-49) context manager:
- Configurable isolation level (default: `READ COMMITTED`)
- 5-second `lock_timeout` per transaction
- Automatic rollback on exception
- Connection always returned clean

### 3.4 Request Flow

```
Client Request
  → CorrelationIDMiddleware (UUID generation, timing)
    → FastAPI Router (path matching)
      → Auth Dependency (JWT/session validation, role check)
        → Service Layer (business logic, validation)
          → get_transaction() → PostgreSQL (raw SQL)
        ← Result dict
      ← Pydantic response model
    ← X-Correlation-ID header
  ← JSON response
```

