## 6. Authentication System

### 6.1 Flow

```
Browser → GET /api/auth/login
  → Redirect to Google OAuth consent page
  → Google callback → GET /api/auth/callback
    → Verify ID token
    → Validate email domain (@hindustanuniv.ac.in)
    → Lookup/create staff in database
    → Create session (Redis/memory)
    → Generate JWT (PyJWT, HS256)
    → Set faculty_session cookie + redirect with ?token=JWT
```

### 6.2 Auth Dependencies (per-request)

[get_current_user](file:///c:/Users/itsni/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/faculty_selection/app/auth/dependencies.py):
1. Check `Authorization: Bearer <JWT>` header → decode JWT
2. Else check `faculty_session` cookie → lookup session
3. If `DEV_AUTH_BYPASS=true` (dev only) → auto-login as coordinator
4. **Always** performs fresh DB lookup for user role (never trusts token role)

### 6.3 Roles

| Role | Source | Grants Access To |
|---|---|---|
| [coordinator](file:///c:/Users/itsni/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/faculty_selection/app/auth/router.py#52-86) | `staff.is_coordinator = true` | All admin, allocation, reports, staff endpoints |
| `hod` | `staff.designation = 'HOD'` | Same as coordinator (resolved from DB) |
| [faculty](file:///c:/Users/itsni/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/faculty_selection/app/reports/router.py#31-41) | Default | Preferences, selection, dashboard |

### 6.4 Security Controls

- Email domain validation: `@hindustanuniv.ac.in` enforced in production
- `DEV_AUTH_BYPASS` **blocked at startup** in production (`RuntimeError` raised)
- Session cookie: `HttpOnly`, `Secure` (production), `SameSite=Lax`
- JWT expiration: configurable via `SESSION_EXPIRATION_HOURS` (default: 4)

