## 7. Allocation Engine

**Location**: [app/allocation/service.py](file:///c:/Users/itsni/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/faculty_selection/app/allocation/service.py) (517 lines)

### 7.1 Three-Stage Pipeline

```
Stage 1: Preference-1 Pass
  → Allocate each faculty's preference-1 subject (if shift-compatible and under norm)

Stage 2: Preferences 2–5 Pass
  → Iterate preferences 2-5 in order, allocate if constraints pass

Stage 3: Final Pass (Unallocated Subjects)
  → Assign remaining subjects to lowest-load compatible faculty
```

### 7.2 Constraints Enforced

| Rule | Description |
|---|---|
| **Shift compatibility** | SHIFT1 faculty ↔ shift=1 offerings, SHIFT2 ↔ shift=2, SHIFT1+SHIFT2 ↔ both |
| **Workload norm** | Faculty's `tch_norm` not exceeded (COALESCE to 16 if null) |
| **Multi-section** | Faculty cannot teach same course code multiple times |
| **Active cycle** | Requires an active `academic_cycle` |

### 7.3 Side Effects

- Clears existing [allocation](file:///c:/Users/itsni/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/faculty_selection/app/allocation/router.py#32-86) rows for the active cycle before re-running
- Updates/inserts [workload_summary](file:///c:/Users/itsni/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/faculty_selection/app/admin/router.py#115-126) rows
- Logs `ALLOCATION_RUN` to `audit_log`

---

## 8. Preference Validation Rules

**Location**: [app/preference/service.py](file:///c:/Users/itsni/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/faculty_selection/app/preference/service.py) (394 lines)

| Rule ID | Name | Logic |
|---|---|---|
| PREF-01 | Range | `preference_number` must be 1–5 |
| PREF-02 | Offering uniqueness | No two faculty may assign same pref# to same offering |
| PREF-03 | Faculty uniqueness | Faculty cannot reuse same pref# |
| PREF-04 | Max count | Maximum 5 preferences per faculty |
| PREF-DUP | Duplicate guard | Faculty cannot prefer same offering twice |
| SHIFT-01 | Shift compatibility | Faculty shift must match offering shift |
| CT-01 | Class teacher | Class teacher's pref=1 must match their assigned class |

**Window guard**: Preferences only accepted when a `selection_window` has `status = 'OPEN'`.

---

## 9. FCFS Subject Selection System

**Location**: [app/selection/transactions.py](file:///c:/Users/itsni/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/faculty_selection/app/selection/transactions.py) (423 lines)

### 9.1 Advisory Lock Ordering (FROZEN)

```
1. FOR SHARE    → Window validation (status='OPEN', batch/spec scoping)
2. FOR SHARE    → Eligibility verification (staff_assignment check)
3. pg_advisory_xact_lock(staff_id)          → Staff-level serialization
4. pg_advisory_xact_lock(staff_id, window_id) → Staff+window serialization
5. FOR UPDATE   → Quota check (max_subjects_per_staff)
6. FOR UPDATE   → Slot number assignment
7. INSERT       → FCFS claim via ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING
8. INSERT       → Audit log
```

### 9.2 FCFS Guarantee

The `uq_subject_selected` partial unique index ensures **only one `SELECTED` status per subject**. The `ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING` returns NULL if the subject was already taken.

### 9.3 Change Subject Transaction

Atomic UPDATE swaps `subject_id` on existing row, preserving `staff_slot_number` immutably.

### 9.4 Error Handling

- SQLSTATE `40P01` (deadlock) → "Concurrent change detected, please try again"
- SQLSTATE `55P03` (lock timeout) → Same message
- All other exceptions re-raised for HTTP error mapping

