## 14. Audit Log Action Types

The `audit_log.action_type` constraint (final form from migration 009):

```
SUBJECT_SELECTED, SUBJECT_DESELECTED,
SELECTION_LOCKED, SELECTION_UNLOCKED,
COORDINATOR_OVERRIDE,
WINDOW_CREATED, WINDOW_SCHEDULED, WINDOW_OPENED, WINDOW_CLOSED, WINDOW_ARCHIVED,
PREFERENCE_SUBMITTED, PREFERENCE_CLEARED,
ALLOCATION_RUN, ALLOCATION_OVERRIDE, ALLOCATION_REASSIGN,
ALLOCATION_FREEZE, ALLOCATION_UNFREEZE
```

> **Note**: There is a **constraint conflict** between migrations 008 and 009. Migration 008 defines action types like `SELECT`, `CHANGE`, `OVERRIDE`, while 009 replaces them with `SUBJECT_SELECTED`, `COORDINATOR_OVERRIDE`, etc. The **last applied** (009) is the authoritative set. Backend code (e.g., [selection/transactions.py](file:///c:/Users/itsni/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/faculty_selection/app/selection/transactions.py)) still references old types like `'SELECT'`, `'CHANGE'`, `'OVERRIDE'` — this is a **known inconsistency**.

